---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/privy-vs-justuno';
const title = 'Privy vs Justuno for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare onsite targeting and signup quality while keeping the downstream email sender explicit.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Which product converts better?",
    "answer": "This page has no controlled conversion result. Compare a consistent offer and audience, then inspect downstream subscriber quality as well as signup count."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Justuno replace my email sender?",
    "answer": "Do not assume that from its capture integration. Establish where subscribers go and which system sends each marketing journey."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should the mobile review include?",
    "answer": "Inspect readability, close controls, keyboard interaction, duplicate campaign display and interference with existing storefront banners on your actual theme."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Privy vs Justuno</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Privy vs Justuno for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Compare onsite targeting and signup quality while keeping the downstream email sender explicit.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Choose the onsite job first</h2>
        <p>A hypothetical jewelry store wants a less intrusive mobile signup offer while keeping its current email sender. Another store might want capture and marketing messages managed together. Those are different purchases. Privy markets email, SMS and list growth together. Justuno documents Shopify installation and onsite lead capture. Do not assume that Justuno replaces the existing email sender or that a particular popup mechanic guarantees more valuable subscribers.</p>
        <h2>Map the storefront surfaces</h2>
        <p>List product pages, collection pages and cart surfaces separately. Choose the intended audience and offer for each. For a jewelry product page, an invitation to save a wish list or receive care guidance may be more relevant than a blanket discount; that is a creative hypothesis to test. Keep the offer consistent between candidates when comparing tooling, otherwise you are comparing two incentives as well as two products.</p>
        <h2>Propose a clean capture experiment</h2>
        <p>Assign eligible visitors consistently to one version and avoid showing two competing popups in the same visit. Define signup as a confirmed eligible subscriber, not simply a submitted address. Record device and traffic source so a change in mobile traffic does not masquerade as a tool improvement. Decide the observation period from traffic and purchase timing; there is no universal two-week or ninety-day requirement.</p>
        <h2>Evaluate downstream quality</h2>
        <p>Follow the signup cohort through the same welcome message and offer redemption. Review purchases, unsubscribe signals and discount cost alongside raw signup volume. More addresses can be a poor trade if the offer attracts people who have no interest in the catalog. This is a measurement plan, not a claim that gamification creates bad subscribers or that either vendor has won a test.</p>
        <h2>Inspect installation and mobile behavior</h2>
        <p>Justuno documents automatic addition of embed, conversion and cart code through its Shopify app. Check the actual theme setup for duplicate legacy snippets before enabling another campaign. In a proposed preview exercise, inspect close controls, keyboard focus, offer readability and interaction with existing banners on your important devices. A documented installation path does not certify performance or accessibility on your theme.</p>
        <h2>Make the sender handoff observable</h2>
        <p>Identify the destination list and the permission and acquisition fields that must arrive with a signup. Use an approved test identity to inspect the destination record, welcome eligibility and unsubscribe path. Do not infer a supported Privy-to-Justuno connection or email automation parity from both products appearing in Shopify. Keep one welcome owner and document how campaign shutdown stops new entries.</p>
        <h2>Decision and cost</h2>
        <p>Compare the current quoted allowance, traffic definition, feature access and seasonal overage treatment, plus the retained email platform. Choose Justuno if its demonstrated onsite configuration and sender handoff fit your capture program. Choose Privy if its combined marketing setup meets the job with acceptable operating work. Neither recommendation depends on an arbitrary store-revenue band, fabricated conversion benchmark or forced email migration at a fixed order count. No campaign experiment was run for this article.</p>
        <h2>Primary documentation</h2>
        <p>Product scope checked against primary material on November 25, 2026. Documentation establishes advertised capabilities, not results for this store.</p>
        <ul><li><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/">Privy product scope</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/511-install-justuno-shopify">Justuno Shopify installation</a></li></ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-privy">Omnisend vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-privy">Klaviyo vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Privy vs Justuno FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
